---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';

export const prerender = true;
---
<SiteLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="How this website and Alec Wantoch's Google OAuth client for Omamail handle your information, account access, and privacy choices." noindex>
  <article aria-labelledby="privacy-heading" class="mb-12">
    <h1 id="privacy-heading" class="font-semibold text-2xl mb-2 tracking-tighter">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-neutral-400">Effective <time datetime="2026-11-16">November 16, 2026</time></p>
    <div class="prose leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        I'm Alec M. Wantoch. This policy covers this website and the Google OAuth
        client I provide for use with <a href="https://github.com/huacnlee/omamail">Omamail</a>,
        an independently developed, open-source desktop email and calendar app.
        Questions or privacy requests can be sent to <a href="mailto:alec@wantoch.com">alec@wantoch.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Google account access</h2>
      <p>
        Omamail connects your computer directly to Google. Signing in authorizes
        the app to access your account; it does not send your mailbox, calendar,
        or sign-in tokens to me or to this website. Google handles sign-in, and
        Omamail does not receive your Google password.
      </p>
      <p>The Google permissions Omamail requests are:</p>
      <dl class="space-y-4">
        <div>
          <dt class="font-mono text-sm break-all">https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.modify</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1 text-neutral-200">Read messages, threads, attachments, and labels; search and organize mail; save drafts; and apply changes such as archiving, marking read, or moving messages to trash.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="font-mono text-sm break-all">https://www.googleapis.com/auth/gmail.send</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1 text-neutral-200">Send the emails and replies you choose to send.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="font-mono text-sm break-all">https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.events</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1 text-neutral-200">Read calendar events and invitations, respond to invitations, and create, update, or delete events when you use those features.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="font-mono text-sm break-all">https://www.googleapis.com/auth/calendar.calendarlist.readonly</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1 text-neutral-200">List your calendars so you can choose which calendar to use.</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
      <p>
        The app also reads your account's email address to identify your mailbox.
        Google data is used to provide the email and calendar features you request.
      </p>

      <h2>Storage and security</h2>
      <p>
        Omamail keeps its data on your device. Refresh tokens are stored in your
        operating system's credential store, such as the Linux keyring. Mail,
        attachments, calendar data, drafts, and settings may be stored locally
        so the app can load quickly and work offline. Google API requests use
        encrypted HTTPS connections. I do not operate a server that stores this data.
      </p>

      <h2>Sharing and optional AI features</h2>
      <p>
        Using email and calendar features sends the necessary data directly to
        Google, including messages you send and event changes you make. If you
        choose to use Omamail's AI assistance, the message or conversation you
        select and your request are passed to the assistant you configured.
        That provider processes them under its own terms, privacy policy, and
        your account settings. I do not receive that content.
      </p>
      <p>
        Loading remote images in a message or following a link contacts the
        sender's or destination's servers, which may receive your IP address
        and other request information.
      </p>

      <h2>Google API Limited Use</h2>
      <p>
        The use and transfer of information received from Google APIs through
        this OAuth client will adhere to the
        <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
        including its Limited Use requirements, and the
        <a href="https://developers.google.com/workspace/workspace-api-user-data-developer-policy">Google Workspace API User Data and Developer Policy</a>.
        Google user data is not sold, used for advertising, or used to develop
        or train generalized AI or machine learning models. Access and transfers
        are limited to providing the features you request and the exceptions
        those policies allow. I do not access or read your Google data through
        this client.
      </p>

      <h2>Disconnecting and deleting data</h2>
      <p>
        Signing out of an account in Omamail removes its stored refresh token.
        You can also revoke access from your
        <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">Google Account permissions</a>.
        Local caches and settings may remain after signing out or uninstalling;
        remove Omamail's local application data to delete them. On Linux, cached
        data is normally in <code>~/.cache/omamail</code>. Removing local data
        does not delete messages or events stored by Google. I have no server
        copy of your Google data to delete.
      </p>

      <h2>This website</h2>
      <p>
        If you subscribe to my journal, your email address is stored with Kit
        to send the updates you requested. You can unsubscribe using the link
        in an email or contact me to request deletion. If you email me, I keep
        your message as needed to respond and handle your request.
      </p>
      <p>
        This site is hosted on Vercel and uses Vercel Analytics, Vercel Speed
        Insights, and Google Analytics to understand visits and performance.
        These services may process request and usage information such as your
        IP address, browser, device, pages visited, and timing data. Google
        Analytics may use cookies. Website analytics do not receive your
        Omamail messages, calendar data, or OAuth tokens.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>This website and OAuth client are not directed to children under 13. I do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13.</p>

      <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
      <p>
        Updates will be posted here with a new effective date. If the way this
        OAuth client uses Google data changes, I will obtain any consent Google
        requires before using it for a new purpose. For questions or requests,
        email <a href="mailto:alec@wantoch.com">alec@wantoch.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
